	Actually, I have droped the idea of a supers as a class. Irac (Ira 
Carmel) and I worked out an idea for a new stationary item the phone 
booth. Going inside would be like entering a trapper, accept you could 
exit at any time unless the door got stuck. Taking off your armor and 
puting it back on inside a phone booth would the off chance of changing 
you into a hero. Become a hero entails increasing some stats, and gaining 
some intrinsics (including one that you normaly can only get from items.) 
We also thought that if you put in a gold piece, you could make a call. 
Some bad things could happen (mostly summoning monsters, or hari-crishnas) 
but you might be able to order a pizza or talk to Sally the Succubus, or 
even get the home shoping network. If you got the home shopping, you could 
use a card to order things on credit (otherwise it's strictly COD) but if 
any gold you earned would be taken away untill you payed off the debt. If 
you didn't pay off the debt soon enough you woul dhave interest charges 
,and pretty soon Guido the Deamon would come and take away all your 
possestions (or enough top pay off the debt).
	The other idea was to have a locked phone booth that could only be 
opened with a skeliton key. This would be the Doctor's TARDIS, and would 
lead to an independat level like the castle. It could also contain the 
Master's TARDIS, and set up an infinite loop (well sort of).

   The idea behind the super-hero, was a chance to get intrinsics that 
normally can't be gained except through items. The one bad thing about 
being a super would be that Shopkeepers would recognize you, and try to 
get you to pay more money for stuff. They would be more understanding 
about broken doors. I can immagine a shopkeeper saying "Hey aren't you 
<hero name>; could I have your autograph?" They would also say "For a hero 
like you only <higher price> for this <item name>."
 
